=== 3. THE PRE-CHECK -- HOW BIG IS THE SEASONAL ATMOSPHERIC d13C SIGNAL? ===
  A seasonal SST cycle modulates eps_up, which modulates the ISOTOPIC RATIO
  of the evasion limb only. For a sinusoid at omega = 2*pi/yr, well above the
  air-sea relaxation rate F_up/M_atm, the atmospheric response is
      amplitude(d13C_atm) = F_up * amplitude(eps_up) / (M_atm * omega)
  ⚠ ANALYTIC AND HEMISPHERICALLY LOCAL: it ignores interhemispheric exchange
    and the ocean's own d13C response, both of which DAMP it. So this is an
    UPPER bound on the term, which is the right side to err on for a gate
    whose purpose is to kill a mechanism.

  hem        F_up      M_atm  d eps/dT   amp eps | amp d13C_atm     OBSERVED    ratio
           GtC/yr        GtC  permil/K    permil |   permil p-p   permil p-p         
  NH        45.51     452.38   +0.1038    0.1110 |      0.00355       0.3567   0.0100
  SH        65.34     450.30   +0.1039    0.0558 |      0.00258       0.0337   0.0766

  stations: NH -> MLO, SH -> SPO (the two d13c_seasonal_* rows)
  GATE M: global atmosphere 902.7 GtC at 425.0 ppm ⇒ 2.1240 GtC/ppm vs the constant 2.1240 -> PASS


=== 3b. AGAINST THE ROWS' RESIDUAL -- WHICH IS WHAT sec.3's VERDICT ASKS FOR ===
  7 % of an OBSERVABLE is not the same statement as 7 % of what the model
  gets WRONG on that observable. And an amplitude alone cannot say whether a
  term helps: two vectors of the same size ADD or CANCEL by their PHASE.

  ⚠ THE RESPONSE PHASE IS DERIVED, NOT MEASURED. eps_up rises with SST, so
    the evasion limb sends ISOTOPICALLY HEAVIER carbon up in local summer;
    the atmosphere INTEGRATES that, so its anomaly lags the SST peak by a
    quarter cycle. The model's SST peaks at month 3.5 + CCX_SST_SEAS_LAG + 3
    in the NH and six months later in the SH (the sign flip at model.R:1421).

  hem       model     mo |   observed     mo |   RESIDUAL     mo |    omitted     mo |  |term|/
           permil        |     permil        |     permil        |     permil        |  |resid|
  NH       0.3463   9.52 |     0.3567   9.41 |     0.0240   1.31 |    0.00355  10.82 |    0.148
  SH       0.0643   3.12 |     0.0337   3.24 |     0.0307   2.99 |    0.00258   4.82 |    0.084

  and what the term would DO to each residual, added as a vector:
  NH   (MLO) residual 0.0240 -> 0.0252 permil  (+4.85 %)  phase gap -2.49 months ⇒ GROWS it
  SH   (SPO) residual 0.0307 -> 0.0323 permil  (+5.04 %)  phase gap +1.83 months ⇒ GROWS it


=== 4. SCORED ===
  the omitted term is 1.00 % (NH) / 7.66 % (SH) of the OBSERVED seasonal d13C.
  that is 1.1 orders of magnitude below the observable at its largest.
  against the ROWS' RESIDUAL it is 14.8 % (NH) / 8.4 % (SH).

  ⚠ SIGN ROBUSTNESS. The effect goes as |term| x cos(phase gap), so it flips
    at a gap of 3.00 months. The gaps and their margins:
      NH  gap -2.49 mo, 0.51 mo from the flip -> the sign is ⚠ MARGINAL
      SH  gap +1.83 mo, 1.17 mo from the flip -> the sign is robust

  ⇒ NOT THE EXPLANATION. The term is 8-15 % of what the model already gets 
    WRONG on the two rows that carry the veto, and at the derived phase it 
    moves both residuals the WRONG WAY by ~5 %. A flag worth -12.2 prior-sd 
    cannot be paid for out of a term this size whichever way it points. 
    ⇒ IT IS REAL PHYSICS AND IT IS STILL NOT THE ANSWER -- which is exactly 
      the outcome handoff §5 said was worth an afternoon rather than a refit.

  ⛔ AND THE MEAN VALUE IS A SEPARATE QUESTION FROM THE SLOPE. Zhang puts
     eps_up at -8.66 / -8.87 permil (NH/SH) against the model's hardcoded -10.00;
     that is a CONSTANT offset on the evasion limb, it moves the steady-state
     d_ml - d_atm, and it is the 5a question. It is NOT priced here.

